      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/oaktree/{size}/2287_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-10-31T00:31:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ah. Games Keep. I purchased the original printing of Sentinels there many moons ago. I live in the city so the Keep is not far. I also recommend Redcaps Corner here in the city as another great place to game.&nbsp;If you are planning on attending, I might try and attend myself!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Redcaps Corner is around 38th Street IIRC?&nbsp; Been there once back around when they opened.&nbsp; I live in the city as well, but get out to West Chester every other week or so.&nbsp; There's also gaming up in Langhorne at the Oxford Valley Mall a few Saturdays a month, but I have not been up there for a while.&nbsp; Haven't checked out what the gaming scene is in city for a while.</p>",
